 "response": "Memol's current budget is **$1886K**.\n\n**How it was worked out**\n- The only record that sets the budget outright is #0001, at $1090K. Every later Finance Office budget update was applied in order. Messages from other departments were ignored, as were Finance notes that do not change the budget (audits, cost centre codes, purchase orders, reminders).\n- Withdrawals were resolved as chains. A withdrawal that was itself withdrawn stops counting, and its original target applies again. Examples:\n  - **#0002 (\u2212$51K) applies:** its withdrawal #0019 was withdrawn by #0364.\n  - **#0055 (+$543K) applies:** #0349 was withdrawn by #0351. That leaves #0338 in force, which cancels #0056, the withdrawal of #0055.\n  - **#0241 (\u2212$274K) does not apply:** #0721 was withdrawn by #0853. That keeps #0718 in force, which cancels #0491. That leaves #0249, which withdraws #0241.\n  - **#0024 (+$433K) does not apply:** #1121 was withdrawn by #1307, so #0274's withdrawal of #0024 stands.\n- About 130 updates ended up withdrawn. The remaining effective changes were added one by one to the starting $1090K, giving $1886K.\n\nThis was a single manual running total over about 600 entries. I did not do a separate second calculation. I did re-scan the withdrawals once and found one I had missed (#0877, withdrawing #0536 +$483K), which I then excluded.\n\nANSWER: $1886K",
